  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nCanadian high pressure will build over the region today, \ndelivering dry weather and cooler temperatures to the area for\nthe start of the week. Temperatures will generally be in the low\nto mid 60s today with highs warming by a couple of degrees\nduring the day Tuesday. Radiational cooling will be most\nefficient with the high directly overhead tonight and widespread\nlows in the upper 30s to around 40 degrees are expected with\nlocally warmer temps likely along the immediate lakeshore.\nTypical cold spots across interior NE OH and NW PA will likely \ndip into the mid 30s, although there's still some potential for \nscattered cloud cover which would limit frost coverage. Have\nheld off on the issuance on a Frost Advisory at this point since\ncoverage should be scattered, but will reassess throughout the\nday.\n\nTemperatures will warm further on Wednesday as the high shifts \neast and a warm front crosses the area. The next cold front will\npush across the area towards the end of the week, but guidance \nfavors a dry frontal passage.",
